WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.707
A common source of confusion is that data often arrives as text.

00:00:04.707 --> 00:00:13.997
Forms, CSV files, APIs, and user input frequently give us strings even when the characters look numeric.

00:00:13.997 --> 00:00:21.307
The text “29.99” looks like a price to us, but Python may still treat it as a string.

00:00:21.769 --> 00:00:26.856
Before doing arithmetic, we convert the text to an appropriate numeric type.

00:00:26.856 --> 00:00:32.431
Float is useful for decimal values, while int is useful for whole numbers.

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:37.640
The pattern is simple: receive text, convert it, then calculate.
